  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is statistical calibration and confounder handling for compositional and high-dimensional omics. Two benchmarks compare methods systematically: 71 single-cohort and 63 multi-cohort confounder-aware microbiome differential abundance strategies (releasing xConDA), and 12 differential composition methods on three population-scale scRNA-seq datasets using real data, permutations and simulations. ssGSEA3.0 replaces feature-label permutation with feature-level bootstrap resampling for per-sample significance. Method development addresses compositional structure directly: RoDPAA integrates multi-view microbiome data without log-ratio transforms, IsoVita learns compositional features along continuous covariates with change point and spline tests, and a structural equation framework links microbiome cohorts to smaller paired metabolome data using ALR. TensorPLS extends PLS-DA to longitudinal omics with nested cross-validation. New here is the emphasis on empirical calibration across cohort settings and alternatives to permutation nulls.",
